# Edge-level redirect for the bare root — without this, Astro's static build serves
# dist/index.html which is just a meta-refresh + JS redirect page, so visitors see a
# visible "Redirecting from / to /en/" flash before the real homepage loads.
/ /en/ 301

# Privacy/Disclaimer are legal boilerplate with one canonical English page (never
# actually translated per-locale — see cards.ts/index.astro commit history). The
# hi/hinglish routes still build as Astro meta-refresh redirect stubs so old
# indexed URLs don't 404, but that means a visible flash same as the root case
# above — so redirect at the edge before that stub is served.
/hi/privacy/ /en/privacy/ 301
/hi/disclaimer/ /en/disclaimer/ 301
/hinglish/privacy/ /en/privacy/ 301
/hinglish/disclaimer/ /en/disclaimer/ 301
